{"page": 37, "text": "Gross profit increased by $25.0 million to $218.0 million, or 13.0%, for the three months ended September 30, 2026, compared to the three months ended September 30, 2025. Our gross profit margin was 74.1% for the three months ended September 30, 2026, compared to 72.2% for the three months ended September 30, 2025. The increase in gross profit was due to increased software subscription revenues and economies of scale resulting from fixed cost arrangements.\nResearch and Development\nResearch and development expense increased by $0.1 million to $53.0 million, or 0.2%, for the three months ended September 30, 2026, compared to the three months ended September 30, 2025. The increase was primarily due to a $2.9 million increase in personnel-related costs and a $1.2 million increase in information technology (\"IT\") related costs, partially offset by a $2.5 million decrease in stock-based compensation expense and a $1.6 million increase in the amount of capitalized time on platform and customer solution enhancements.\nSelling and Marketing\nSelling and marketing expense decreased by $6.2 million to $38.0 million, or 14.0%, for the three months ended September 30, 2026, compared to the three months ended September 30, 2025. This decrease was primarily due to a $2.7 million decrease in stock-based compensation, a $2.0 million decrease in personnel-related costs, and a $1.1 million decrease in professional service costs.\nGeneral and Administrative\nGeneral and administrative expense increased by $3.7 million to $51.0 million, or 7.9%, for the three months ended September 30, 2026, compared to the three months ended September 30, 2025. The increase was primarily due to a $3.7 million increase in professional service costs, a $2.3 million increase in personnel-related costs, and a $1.4 million increase in IT related costs, partially offset by a $2.6 million decrease in stock-based compensation and a $1.1 million decrease in other business taxes.\nAmortization of Intangible Assets\nAmortization of intangible assets was $18.5 million for the three months ended September 30, 2026 and 2025.\nInterest Expense\nInterest expense increased by $2.8 million to $20.9 million, or 15.5%, for the three months ended September 30, 2026, compared to the three months ended September 30, 2025. The increase was primarily due to the interest incurred on an additional $300 million term loan as part of the Fifth Amendment to the 2021 Credit Agreement entered into in December 2025.\nInterest Income\nInterest income increased by $0.3 million to $1.4 million, or 28.2%, for the three months ended September 30, 2026, compared to the three months ended September 30, 2025, primarily reflecting higher interest earned on interest-bearing deposits and money market funds during the three months ended September 30, 2026 compared to the three months ended September 30, 2025.\n30\nOther Income (Expense)\u2014Net\n"}
